{
  "id": "m75l1",
  "title": {
    "es": "Memoización y subproblemas",
    "en": "Memoization and subproblems"
  },
  "theory": {
    "es": [
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "value": "Guardar lo ya calculado"
      },
      {
        "type": "text",
        "value": "La **programación dinámica** resuelve un problema combinando soluciones de subproblemas más pequeños, **guardando** los resultados para no recalcularlos. Subir una escalera de n peldaños (de 1 o 2 en 2) es la suma de las formas de subir n-1 y n-2."
      },
      {
        "type": "code",
        "value": [
          "def escalera(n):",
          "    a, b = 1, 1",
          "    for _ in range(n):",
          "        a, b = b, a + b",
          "    return a",
          "",
          "print(escalera(4))"
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "output",
        "value": [
          "5"
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "note",
        "value": "Es la versión 'de abajo arriba' (tabla) de lo que con recursión harías con @lru_cache."
      }
    ],
    "en": [
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "value": "Storing what's already computed"
      },
      {
        "type": "text",
        "value": "**Dynamic programming** solves a problem by combining solutions of smaller subproblems, **storing** the results to avoid recomputing. Climbing a staircase of n steps (1 or 2 at a time) is the sum of the ways to climb n-1 and n-2."
      },
      {
        "type": "code",
        "value": [
          "def escalera(n):",
          "    a, b = 1, 1",
          "    for _ in range(n):",
          "        a, b = b, a + b",
          "    return a",
          "",
          "print(escalera(4))"
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "output",
        "value": [
          "5"
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "note",
        "value": "It's the 'bottom-up' (table) version of what you'd do recursively with @lru_cache."
      }
    ]
  },
  "exercises": [
    {
      "id": "m75l1e1",
      "prompt": {
        "es": "Define `subir_escalera(n)`: nº de formas de subir n peldaños subiendo de 1 o de 2 en 2.",
        "en": "Define `subir_escalera(n)`: number of ways to climb n steps taking 1 or 2 at a time."
      },
      "starter_code": [
        "def subir_escalera(n):",
        "    pass"
      ],
      "solution": [
        "def subir_escalera(n):",
        "    a, b = 1, 1",
        "    for _ in range(n):",
        "        a, b = b, a + b",
        "    return a"
